>
  <h2>Overview</h2>
  <p>
    The Replay feature records a screen capture of your KovaaK's runs and plays
    them back inside RefleK's, letting you watch exactly what happened during
    any scenario — your crosshair placement, target transitions, and overall
    movement — frame by frame.
  </p>

  <h2>How It Works</h2>
  <p>
    When replay recording is enabled, RefleK's captures your screen at a high
    rate during your runs. The capture is saved locally alongside your run data
    and can be played back from the replay viewer.
  </p>

  <h2>Performance & Resource Usage</h2>
  <p>
    Replay is designed to be as performant and resource-efficient as possible.
    The capture pipeline uses GPU encoding to record your screen, so there is no
    significant impact on your CPU or game performance while recording.
  </p>
  <p>
    Even while actively recording a run, the additional RAM usage is only around
    50 MB — the feature is extremely lightweight during capture.
  </p>
  <p>
    During playback, you may notice a higher increase in RAM usage. This is
    because the video is rendered through the webview, which allocates additional
    memory to decode and display the capture smoothly.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Disk space</strong> — capture files are stored locally and will
      accumulate over time; you can delete individual captures after watching
      them from the replay viewer
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>GPU-accelerated capture</strong> — encoding is handled by your
      GPU, keeping CPU overhead to a minimum during recording
    </li>
  </ul>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Tip:</strong> If you're on a system with limited RAM, you can disable
    replay recording per-session or toggle it off entirely in settings while still
    keeping stat tracking and mouse movement analysis active.
  </div>

  <h2>Playback Controls</h2>
  <p>Once a run has a replay capture, you can:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Play / Pause</strong> — watch the run at normal speed</li>
    <li><strong>Speed control</strong> — slow down to study movements or speed up to skip through</li>
    <li><strong>Scrub</strong> — jump to any moment in the run</li>
    <li><strong>Full-screen mode</strong> — expand the replay for a closer look</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="warning">
    <strong>Anticheat Warning:</strong> Replay captures your screen
    using low-level system APIs. While RefleK's is designed to work safely with
    KovaaK's, some kernel-level anticheat systems in other games (such as Vanguard
    or FACEIT) may misinterpret screen capture calls as intrusive behavior. If you
    play games with aggressive anticheats, consider closing RefleK's before
    launching those games or disable replay recording when not using KovaaK's.
  </div>

  <h2>Data & Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    All replay captures are stored locally on your machine. RefleK's does not
    upload or share your screen captures anywhere. You can delete individual
    captures after watching them from the replay viewer.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Note:</strong> Replay capture is Windows-only due to platform-specific
    APIs.
  </div>
